<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco Pereira Coutinho</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1547</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco Pereira Coutinho was a Portuguese nobleman and veteran of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> who received the hereditary Captaincy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-all-saints">Bay of All Saints</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> III in 1534. His settlement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahia">Bahia</a> struggled and came into conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupinamba">Tupinambá</a>, who killed him in 1547. The crown bought back the captaincy, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> was founded there in 1549 as the seat of royal government.</p></div>
